  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are the roots of the equation $x^2-x+1=0$, then $\\alpha^{2009}+\\beta^{2009}=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "yu6Kc",
      "text": "\n$-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEkSc",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zAy7o",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tGNpY",
      "text": "\n$-2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^2-x+1=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{1-4}}{2}$\n$x=\\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{3} i}{2}$\n$\\alpha=\\frac{1}{2}+i \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\quad \\beta=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{i \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n$\\alpha=\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{3}+i \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\quad \\beta=\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{3}-i \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\n$\\alpha^{2009}+\\beta^{2009}=2 \\cos 2009\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)$\n$=2 \\cos \\left[668 \\pi+\\pi+\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right]=2 \\cos \\left(\\pi+\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right)$\n$=-2 \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}=-2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=1$",
    "image": null
  },
